      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Trimethyllysine hydroxylase (TMLH) catalyses C-3 hydroxylation of Nε-trimethyllysine in the first step of carnitine biosynthesis in humans. Studies on TMLH have been hampered by the lack of established chemical methods. We report that an Nε-trimethyllysine analogue that contains the fluoromethyl group can be used as a 1H and 19F NMR probe for studies on TMLH catalysis."},
